{
 "id": "2026-11-17-b",
 "title": "Voyager 1 is one light-DAY away. We still hear it 📡",
 "description": "On 18 November 2026 Voyager 1 becomes the first human-made object one light-day from Earth: 25.9 billion km, so a 'hello' takes a day to arrive and the reply another day. Its radio runs on about 22 watts (a fridge bulb), and the signal reaches us weaker than a billionth of a billionth of a watt, yet NASA's 70 m dishes with super-cold amplifiers still catch it. The catch: its plutonium power drops ~4 W a year, so instruments are being switched off (two left); the team hopes to keep one running into the 2030s.\n\nSources: EarthSky; NASA/JPL; WAMC (April 2026); MakeTechEasier on how the Deep Space Network hears Voyager.",
